From 34985981abe4fd8ecd288b88d46176852eab69f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luigi Vanfretti <luigi.vanfretti@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 18:16:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] build(IEEE_CIGRE): no floating-point contraction on gcc
 and clang

On 64-bit ARM every compiler has fused multiply-add instructions and clang
contracts a*b+c into them by default, so the DLL's C code rounds once where
the x86-64 builds round twice. Measured with System Modeler 14.3 on Apple
Silicon: the start-up transient of GFM_GFL_IBR amplifies those last-bit
differences into a different trajectory (out[6] off by 0.38 pu at 5.9 ms, P
by up to 26 MW on the 10 MVA base in the first 0.4 s of the GFL tests, extra
current-zero events), whereas with -ffp-contract=off the ARM run equals the
Windows round-2 result to 2e-9 relative, the same order as Linux x86-64
against Windows. SCRX9 and the network-only tests were unaffected.
-ffp-contract=off is added for every non-MSVC compiler; MSVC does not
contract under its default /fp:precise.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../Resources/C-Sources/IEEE_CIGRE/CMakeLists.txt     | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/OpenIPSL/Resources/C-Sources/IEEE_CIGRE/CMakeLists.txt b/OpenIPSL/Resources/C-Sources/IEEE_CIGRE/CMakeLists.txt
index 0897f355..4b2e66d9 100644
--- a/OpenIPSL/Resources/C-Sources/IEEE_CIGRE/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/OpenIPSL/Resources/C-Sources/IEEE_CIGRE/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -84,6 +84,17 @@ else()
   set(_oipsl_warnings -Wall -Wextra)
 endif()
 
+# No floating-point contraction: clang (and gcc outside ISO C mode) fuses a*b+c into one fused multiply-add
+# wherever the target has it (every 64-bit ARM; x86-64 only with -mfma). The fused result is rounded once
+# instead of twice, so the same C source gives different last bits on ARM and on x86-64. Measured on Apple
+# Silicon (2026-10-31): GFM_GFL_IBR's start-up transient amplifies that to a visibly different trajectory
+# (P off by up to 2.6 Sbase in the first 0.4 s of the GFL tests, several extra current-zero events), while with
+# -ffp-contract=off the ARM results equal the x86-64 ones to 2e-9 relative, the same as Linux against Windows.
+# MSVC does not contract under its default /fp:precise.
+if(NOT MSVC)
+  list(APPEND _oipsl_warnings -ffp-contract=off)
+endif()
+
 # oipsl_target_settings(<target>): reproducible MSVC builds (/Brepro: no time stamps in the PE files, so a
 # rebuild of the same sources gives bit-identical DLLs and import libraries)
 function(oipsl_target_settings target)
